=== 1. assignment values expand after each unquoted colon
a:/h/b
/h:/h/c:d~:~e:/h
a:/p:/o
a:/h:/h
a::/h
/h/b:/h
/usr/bin:/h/bin
=== 2. quoted or partly quoted prefixes stay literal
a:~/b
a:~/b
a:~/b
a:~/b
~/b
a:~:b
a:~x
a=~
~/h
=== 3. append, element and keyed array assignments
a:/h
x:~ /h
x:~ q:/h
k:/h x=~
/h:/h
=== 4. prefix assignments
a:/h
=== 5. words spelled like assignments
a:~/b x=a:/h/b y=/h a+=/h a[1]=x:/h e==~
1=~ a-b=~ --opt=~ b:=~ d=~
a:/h/b
a:/h/b
a:/h/b
/h:/h
a=/h
b:~
case pattern matched
=== 6. command words
/h /h/x /h:x /h/a:~ /p /o ~ ~
~/h
=== 7. the expansion is not split or globbed
n=1 [/s p]
a:/s p
/* /*/x
n=1 []
